cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use SDIP in a publication, please cite both the software and the
  specification. The specification is the contribution; the software implements it.
title: "SDIP — Seismic Data Ingestion & Preparation"
abstract: >-
  SEG-Y to MDIO/Zarr v3 conversion with a machine-checkable proof of 1-1 equivalence
  to the source. SDIP defines a five-plane Equivalence Contract — textual header,
  binary header, trace header, sample, and cardinality/ordering — and issues a
  machine-readable Equivalence Certificate per ingestion. Comparisons are exact:
  array equality or byte equality, never tolerance-based. Every ingestion runs against
  a trace-header specification covering bytes 1-240 with zero gaps and zero overlaps,
  so proprietary and undocumented byte locations survive the crossing. Output is a
  plain Zarr v3 store readable with stock zarr or xarray with neither SDIP nor MDIO
  installed. The product is not the file; the product is the file plus the proof.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/zahidaramai/sdip"
url: "https://github.com/zahidaramai/sdip"
keywords:
  - SEG-Y
  - MDIO
  - Zarr
  - seismic
  - geophysics
  - lossless conversion
  - data validation
  - provenance
  - reproducibility
  - cloud-native

